# The base's pad pressure in PERF mode with RTRG held: the RETRIG menu passes pad pressure on, so pad 1's
# pressure moves performance 1's amount (a u16 at 0x8000e57c, the pressure byte times 128, written through
# 0x400b2c6a) as it does without RTRG. Stock froze it while RTRG was held. Pressure 0 brings it back.
# Enters PERF mode with PERF and leaves it with PERF (the screen does not change: where pressure goes shows it).
name: pad-pressure-perf-rtrg
state: changes

key PERF
wait 500
hold RTRG
wait 300
pad BD down 100
wait 300
pad BD pressure 60
wait 300
mem p60 0x8000e57c 2
pad BD pressure 0
wait 300
mem p0 0x8000e57c 2
pad BD up
wait 300
release RTRG
wait 300
key PERF
wait 500
pad BD down 100                     # PERF again: back on the pad page, pressure goes to BD again
wait 300
pad BD pressure 60
wait 300
mem off60 0x8000e57c 2
mem at60 0x800067de 2
pad BD pressure 0
pad BD up
wait 300
expect p60 == 1e00
expect p0 == 0000
expect off60 == 0000
expect at60 == 1e00
